From 1b3faa9af351b15a3482e2e4b7ada21f41525a2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MicroNUX <micronux@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:33:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 32/48] video: fbdev: program native DSI panel cold stage

Extend the ABI-v3 one-shot cold_init path so its completed I2C/LDO stage
flows directly into native command-mode DSI panel programming.

Validate the complete pinned JD9365 firmware header, length, record
grammar, bounds, and payload CRC before sending any DCS packet. Bring up
the ESP32-P4 DSI host and D-PHY from the ESP-IDF v6.0.1 register sequence,
release the external controller with PWM held at zero, preserve the
Waveshare parity delay, issue a no-parameter software reset, and execute
all 204 bounded records.

Leave bridge DPI, the DPI clock, GDMA, framebuffer registration, and IRQ
ownership disabled. Enter PANEL_PROGRAMMED_QUIESCENT only after exact
readback. On failure, best-effort return the external controller, DSI,
LDO, and I2C pins to a verified safe state, distinguishing
FAILED_QUIESCENT from FAILED_UNVERIFIED.

Signed-off-by: MicroNUX <micronux@example.invalid>
---
